      "archaeologicalRemains": "substantive",
      "details": "<p><span>The gate\u2019s approximate location is based on an aerial photograph of Nineveh taken in 1929, Corona satellite imagery (1967-68), and Google satellite imagery. Note that most scholarly reconstructions place the A\u0161\u0161ur Gate about 150 m west of the southeast corner (approximate coordinates: 36.3364280, 43.1769084); this is where the <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../960751426\" target=\"_self\" title=\"Sennacherib Gate\">Sennacherib Gate</a> is now thought to have been\u00a0built.</span></p>",
